 "note": "T. C. Passios Elementary School, identified by its own heading on line 1 ('T. C. PASSIOS ELEMENTARY SCHOOL STAFF'). The page is two columns flattened into lines: the left column runs Pre-School, Kindergarten, First to Fourth Grade; the right column runs Special Education, Art, Music, Physical Education, Reading Specialist, Guidance Counselor, Nurse, Office, Administration, Custodians. Because the two columns' rows do not align, a single-name line could belong to either; every such line was assigned by the page image (rendered from the PDF), not by text order -- e.g. Jane Zimmerman (5), Jane Murray (7), Richard Mulligan (18), Lois Davenport (26), Irene Beaulac (34) sit in the right column. No title is printed beside any name, so role_raw is '' and the section heading is grade_or_dept (Administration lists McSheehy and Daukantas without titles). Lines 6, 10, 11, 12, 16, 19, 20, 24, 32, 35, 36 hold a heading in one column and a name in the other, so they appear in both headings and entries. Lines 44-50 are the title, byline and opening of the Middle School Principal's Report (another section) and line 51 is the page number; all ignored."
